---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Inductor"
  description="A coil is a flywheel for charge. Drive it by hand and watch the electrons refuse to start, then refuse to stop, while the magnetic field they wind up around themselves stores every joule it takes to get them moving."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="ind" class="ind-canvas" width="1000" height="880"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Source</label>
        <div class="seg" id="src">
          <button data-s="manual" class="active">Manual</button>
          <button data-s="dc">Battery</button>
          <button data-s="ac">AC</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-v">
        <label><span id="vlab">Drive it yourself</span> <b id="vsval">0.0 V</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="vs" min="-120" max="120" step="1" value="0" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span id="vhint">drag me up and down</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-sw">
        <label>Switch</label>
        <div class="seg" id="mode">
          <button data-m="on" class="active">Closed</button>
          <button data-m="off">Open</button>
          <button data-m="auto">Auto</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-f">
        <label>Frequency <b id="fval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="freq" min="5" max="200" step="5" value="15" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>slow</span><span>fast</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Resistor R <b id="rval">10 Ω</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="r" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="33" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>1 Ω</span><span>1 kΩ</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Turns N <b id="nval">200</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="40" max="500" step="10" value="200" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Core µ<sub>r</sub> <b id="muval">1</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="mu" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="0" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>air</span><span>iron</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Coil area A <b id="aval">4.0 cm²</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="a" min="10" max="120" step="2" value="40" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="fly" /> Fit a flyback diode across the coil</label>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="lines" checked /> Show the magnetic field</label>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">Current</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">Across the coil</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">Inductance</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">Time constant</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">Field inside</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">Flux linkage</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">Energy stored</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        The balls are electrons and their speed is the current itself. Nothing
        about them changes instantly, which is the entire personality of a coil.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start in Manual and shove the slider up hard. The electrons do not jump to
      speed, they <b>accelerate</b>, and while they are speeding up the coil
      takes almost the whole source voltage. A coil with no current in it acts
      like a break in the wire, which is the exact opposite of a capacitor.
    </li>
    <li>
      Hold the slider still. The balls settle to a steady speed, the field stops
      growing, and the voltage across the coil falls to nothing. Once the current
      is constant a coil is just a piece of wire, and the resistor alone decides
      how fast the balls go.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now drop the slider to zero. The electrons <b>keep going</b>, coasting on
      the field, and the coil now pushes instead of resisting to keep them
      moving. Watch the ladder: the coil voltage has flipped sign. It always
      opposes the change, never the current.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn the turns up, then slide the core from air to iron. Inductance climbs
      with <b>N²</b> and again with the core, and the same shove now produces a
      much slower ramp. That is inertia you can dial.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to Battery and open the switch while current is flowing. There is
      nowhere for the electrons to go and they will not stop, so the coil
      produces <b>hundreds of times</b> the battery voltage and drives them
      across the gap as a spark. Tick the flyback diode and try again: the
      current gets a way home and the spike vanishes.
    </li>
    <li>
      In AC, watch the current lag behind the voltage instead of leading it. The
      coil is always a quarter cycle late because voltage sets the rate of
      change, not the value. Raise the frequency and the current shrinks, since
      X<sub>L</sub> = 2πfL: a coil passes DC and blocks high frequencies, which
      is the mirror image of the capacitor.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compare the energy bars with the capacitor's. Here the energy lives in the
      field, ½LI², and it is paid back the moment you try to stop. In the
      capacitor it lives in the field between plates, ½CV², and is paid back the
      moment you let it. Same idea, different quantity held.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  const MU0 = 4 * Math.PI * 1e-7;
  const R_ARC = 5e4; // what an opening switch looks like: a big, lossy gap
  const V_DIODE = 0.7;

  const state = {
    src: 'manual' as 'manual' | 'dc' | 'ac',
    mode: 'on' as 'on' | 'off' | 'auto',
    vs: 0,
    freq: 0.15, // cycles per time constant
    r: 10,
    turns: 200,
    mur: 1,
    area: 4e-4,
    len: 0.1,
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    fly: false,
    lines: true,
  };

  const VMAX = 12;

  let i = 0; // coil current
  let t = 0;
  let tAC = 0;
  let closed = true;
  let train = 0; // how far the queue of electrons has travelled, in pixels
  let wSrc = 0, wRes = 0, wArc = 0;
  let vPeak = 0;
  let hist: { t: number; vs: number; vl: number; i: number }[] = [];
  let histT = 0;
  let clock = 0;

  const ind = () => (MU0 * state.mur * state.turns * state.turns * state.area) / state.len;
  const tauOn = () => ind() / state.r;
  const freqHz = () => state.freq / tauOn();
  /** The switch only exists in battery mode; elsewhere the loop is closed. */
  const isOpen = () => state.src === 'dc' && !closed;
  const rNow = () => (isOpen() ? state.r + (state.fly ? 0 : R_ARC) : state.r);

  function vSource() {
    if (state.src === 'manual') return state.vs;
    if (state.src === 'ac') return state.vs * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * freqHz() * tAC);
    return closed ? state.vs : 0;
  }
  /** What the coil itself is doing: L dI/dt, and the star of the show. */
  function vCoil() {
    if (isOpen() && state.fly) return -(i * state.r + V_DIODE);
    return vSource() - i * rNow();
  }

  function reset() {
    i = 0;
    t = 0;
    tAC = 0;
    train = 0;
    wSrc = wRes = wArc = 0;
    vPeak = 0;
    hist = [];
    histT = 0;
    closed = state.mode !== 'off';
    if (state.src === 'dc' && !closed) i = state.vs / state.r;
  }

  function physics(dtReal: number) {
    const tauNow = ind() / rNow();
    const dt = dtReal * state.rate * (tauNow / 0.9);
    const steps = 12;
    const h = dt / steps;
    for (let s = 0; s < steps; s++) {
      tAC += h;
      const vl = vCoil();
      wSrc += vSource() * i * h;
      wRes += i * i * state.r * h;
      if (isOpen() && !state.fly) wArc += i * i * R_ARC * h;
      i += (vl / ind()) * h;
      if (isOpen() && !state.fly && i < 0) i = 0;
    }
    if (Math.abs(vCoil()) > Math.abs(vPeak)) vPeak = vCoil();
    t += dt;
    histT += dt;
    hist.push({ t: histT, vs: vSource(), vl: vCoil(), i });
    const span = 10 * tauOn();
    while (hist.length > 2 && hist[0].t < histT - span) hist.shift();
    if (state.src === 'dc' && state.mode === 'auto' && t > 5 * (ind() / rNow())) {
      closed = !closed;
      t = 0;
      if (closed) vPeak = 0;
    }
  }

  // --- formatting ------------------------------------------------------------

  function eng(x: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(x);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'],
      [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'], [1e9, 'G'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(x / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }
  const fmtR = (r: number) =>
    r >= 1000 ? (r / 1000).toFixed(r >= 1e4 ? 0 : 2) + ' kΩ' : r.toFixed(r < 10 ? 1 : 0) + ' Ω';

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('ind') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssVar('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const CUR = '#5b8cff';
  const FIELD = '#34d399';
  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const WARM = '#f59e0b';

  const SCENE = { x: 20, y: 76, w: 960, h: 560 };
  const SCOPE = { x: 20, y: 668, w: 620, h: 192 };
  const SIDE = { x: 660, y: 668, w: 320, h: 192 };

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, size = 5) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
    ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.stroke();
    const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a - 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a + 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }
  /** Text over busy artwork needs something to sit on. */
  function chip(
    text: string,
    x: number,
    y: number,
    alpha = 0.8,
    align: CanvasTextAlign = 'center',
    size = 12,
    colour?: string
  ) {
    const w = textWidth(text, size);
    const x0 = align === 'right' ? x - w : align === 'center' ? x - w / 2 : x;
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.globalAlpha = 0.85;
    ctx.fillRect(x0 - 7, y - size * 1.22 - 2, w + 14, size * 1.22 + 9);
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    label(text, x, y, alpha, align, size, colour);
  }

  function head(x: number, y: number, ang: number, size = 6) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x - size * Math.cos(ang - 0.4), y - size * Math.sin(ang - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x - size * Math.cos(ang + 0.4), y - size * Math.sin(ang + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  // --- geometry --------------------------------------------------------------

  type Pt = { x: number; y: number };

  function geom() {
    const cy = SCENE.y + 316;
    const coilW = 400, bump = 46, turns = 8;
    const cx = SCENE.x + 560;
    return { cx, cy, coilW, bump, turns, x0: cx - coilW / 2, x1: cx + coilW / 2 };
  }

  /**
   * The road the electrons take. It runs through every turn of the coil, so a
   * ball you follow really does go round and round the windings.
   */
  function wirePath(): Pt[] {
    const g = geom();
    const yTop = SCENE.y + 62, yBot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 74, xLeft = SCENE.x + 120;
    const pts: Pt[] = [
      { x: xLeft, y: yBot },
      { x: g.x0 - 46, y: yBot },
      { x: g.x0 - 46, y: g.cy },
      { x: g.x0, y: g.cy },
    ];
    // the windings, drawn as the usual row of bumps
    const step = g.coilW / g.turns;
    for (let k = 0; k < g.turns; k++) {
      const c = g.x0 + (k + 0.5) * step;
      for (let s = 0; s <= 10; s++) {
        const a = Math.PI - (Math.PI * s) / 10;
        pts.push({ x: c + Math.cos(a) * (step / 2), y: g.cy - Math.sin(a) * g.bump });
      }
    }
    pts.push({ x: g.x1 + 40, y: g.cy }, { x: g.x1 + 40, y: yTop }, { x: xLeft, y: yTop }, { x: xLeft, y: yBot });
    return pts;
  }

  function pathLength(p: Pt[]) {
    let L = 0;
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) L += Math.hypot(p[k].x - p[k - 1].x, p[k].y - p[k - 1].y);
    return L;
  }
  function pointAt(p: Pt[], d: number): Pt {
    let rem = d;
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) {
      const seg = Math.hypot(p[k].x - p[k - 1].x, p[k].y - p[k - 1].y);
      if (rem <= seg) {
        const f = seg === 0 ? 0 : rem / seg;
        return { x: p[k - 1].x + (p[k].x - p[k - 1].x) * f, y: p[k - 1].y + (p[k].y - p[k - 1].y) * f };
      }
      rem -= seg;
    }
    return p[p.length - 1];
  }
  function strokePath(p: Pt[], alpha = 0.4, lw = 2) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(alpha);
    ctx.lineWidth = lw;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(p[0].x, p[0].y);
    for (let k = 1; k < p.length; k++) ctx.lineTo(p[k].x, p[k].y);
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  // --- the field -------------------------------------------------------------

  const bField = () => (MU0 * state.mur * state.turns * i) / state.len;
  const bRef = () => (MU0 * state.mur * state.turns * (Math.max(1, Math.abs(state.vs)) / state.r)) / state.len;

  function racetrack(cx: number, cy: number, hw: number, hh: number) {
    const r = Math.min(hh, hw);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(cx - hw + r, cy - hh);
    ctx.lineTo(cx + hw - r, cy - hh);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(cx + hw, cy - hh, cx + hw, cy);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(cx + hw, cy + hh, cx + hw - r, cy + hh);
    ctx.lineTo(cx - hw + r, cy + hh);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(cx - hw, cy + hh, cx - hw, cy);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(cx - hw, cy - hh, cx - hw + r, cy - hh);
    ctx.closePath();
  }

  function drawField() {
    const g = geom();
    const b = bField();
    const frac = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, b / Math.max(1e-12, bRef())));
    if (!state.lines || Math.abs(frac) < 0.015) return;
    const dir = i >= 0 ? 1 : -1;
    const n = Math.max(1, Math.round(Math.abs(frac) * 4));
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(52,211,153,${0.18 + 0.45 * Math.abs(frac)})`;
    ctx.fillStyle = ctx.strokeStyle;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    // Field lines wrap the winding: down the bore one way, back round outside.
    for (const side of [-1, 1]) {
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
        const f = (k + 1) / (n + 0.4);
        racetrack(g.cx, g.cy + side * g.bump * 0.5, g.coilW / 2 + 20 + f * 96, 10 + f * (g.bump * 0.5 + 40));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
    // one arrow through the middle says which way it points
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    arrow(g.cx - dir * 60, g.cy, g.cx + dir * 60, g.cy, 9);
    chip(`B = ${eng(Math.abs(b), 'T', 2)}`, g.cx, g.cy + g.bump + 62, 0.9, 'center', 13, FIELD);
  }

  // --- the charges -----------------------------------------------------------

  const BALL = 6.4;
  const SPACING = 40;

  function drawBall(x: number, y: number, alpha = 1) {
    ctx.globalAlpha = alpha;
    ctx.fillStyle = CUR;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(x, y, BALL, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255,255,255,0.55)';
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x - 3, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + 3, y);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
  }

  // --- the source ------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawSource(x: number, y: number) {
    const vsrc = vSource();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 28, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 24; k++) {
        const f = k / 24;
        const px = x - 16 + f * 32;
        const py = y - Math.sin(f * Math.PI * 2) * 10;
        k ? ctx.lineTo(px, py) : ctx.moveTo(px, py);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    } else if (state.src === 'manual') {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 30, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.5);
      ctx.stroke();
      const ang = -Math.PI / 2 + (vsrc / VMAX) * 2.2;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      ctx.lineTo(x + Math.cos(ang) * 22, y + Math.sin(ang) * 22);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x, y, 3.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    } else {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.fillRect(x - 24, y - 22, 48, 44);
      for (let k = 0; k < 2; k++) {
        const yy = y - 8 + k * 16;
        const half = k === 0 ? 17 : 9;
        ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(x - half, yy);
        ctx.lineTo(x + half, yy);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      // the switch, and the spark it draws when it opens on a live coil
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.fillRect(x - 20, y - 62, 46, 32);
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x, y - 58);
      if (closed) ctx.lineTo(x, y - 30);
      else ctx.lineTo(x + 19, y - 42);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.6);
      for (const yy of [y - 58, y - 30]) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x, yy, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      if (isOpen() && !state.fly && Math.abs(vCoil()) > 60) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(245,158,11,${Math.min(0.95, Math.abs(vCoil()) / 500)})`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath();
        for (let k = 0; k <= 6; k++) {
          const f = k / 6;
          const px = x + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 8;
          const py = y - 58 + f * 28 + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 6;
          k ? ctx.lineTo(px, py) : ctx.moveTo(px, py);
        }
        ctx.stroke();
        label('spark', x + 26, y - 44, 0.8, 'left', 11, WARM);
      }
    }
    label(`${vsrc >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${vsrc.toFixed(2)} V`, x + 42, y - 4, 0.85, 'left', 14, WARM);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'you, driving it' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'AC source' : 'battery',
      x + 42,
      y + 14,
      0.45,
      'left',
      11
    );
  }

  function drawResistor(x: number, y: number, len: number) {
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.fillRect(x - 2, y - 13, len + 4, 26);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    const n = 6, amp = 9;
    ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    for (let k = 0; k <= n; k++) ctx.lineTo(x + ((k + 0.5) * len) / (n + 1), y + (k % 2 ? amp : -amp));
    ctx.lineTo(x + len, y);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(fmtR(state.r), x + len / 2, y - 20, 0.55, 'center', 12);
  }

  // --- the voltage ladder ----------------------------------------------------

  /**
   * Source against the resistor's share. What is left over is across the coil,
   * and that leftover is what accelerates the current.
   */
  function drawLadder() {
    const x = SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 96;
    const top = SCENE.y + 78, bot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 96;
    const mid = (top + bot) / 2;
    const Y = (vv: number) => mid - (Math.max(-VMAX, Math.min(VMAX, vv)) / VMAX) * ((bot - top) / 2);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.22);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, top);
    ctx.lineTo(x, bot);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (let vv = -12; vv <= 12; vv += 3) {
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x - 5, Y(vv));
      ctx.lineTo(x + 5, Y(vv));
      ctx.stroke();
      if (vv % 6 === 0) label(`${vv}`, x - 9, Y(vv) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
    const vsrc = vSource(), vr = i * state.r;
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(245,158,11,0.25)';
    ctx.fillRect(x - 7, Math.min(Y(vsrc), Y(vr)), 14, Math.abs(Y(vsrc) - Y(vr)));
    const drawn: number[] = [];
    for (const [vv, col, name] of [
      [vsrc, WARM, 'source'],
      [vr, CUR, 'resistor'],
    ] as [number, string, string][]) {
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x + 7, Y(vv));
      ctx.lineTo(x + 20, Y(vv) - 7);
      ctx.lineTo(x + 20, Y(vv) + 7);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fill();
      // when the two markers land on top of each other, stack the labels
      const clash = drawn.some((yy) => Math.abs(yy - Y(vv)) < 15);
      label(name, x + 25, Y(vv) + (clash ? 17 : 4), 0.8, 'left', 11, col);
      drawn.push(Y(vv));
    }
    label('volts', x, top - 14, 0.45, 'center', 11);
    const dv = vCoil();
    label(`across the coil ${dv >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${dv.toFixed(2)} V`, x - 4, bot + 24, 0.7, 'center', 12, WARM);
    label('this is what speeds the current up', x - 4, bot + 42, 0.4, 'center', 10);
  }

  // --- the scene -------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScene() {
    panel(SCENE, 'INSIDE THE CIRCUIT');
    const g = geom();
    const path = wirePath();
    const xLeft = SCENE.x + 120, yTop = SCENE.y + 62;

    drawField();
    strokePath(path, 0.4);
    drawResistor(xLeft + 150, yTop, 150);
    drawSource(xLeft, g.cy);

    // the queue of electrons, moving at the speed the current says
    const L = pathLength(path);
    const off = ((train % SPACING) + SPACING) % SPACING;
    for (let s = off; s < L; s += SPACING) {
      const p = pointAt(path, s);
      drawBall(p.x, p.y);
    }

    // the core, if there is one worth drawing
    if (state.mur > 1.5) {
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.12);
      rr(g.x0 - 10, g.cy - 12, g.coilW + 20, 24, 5);
      ctx.fill();
      chip(`iron core µ_r = ${state.mur}`, g.x0 - 4, g.cy + g.bump + 30, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    }

    label(`N = ${state.turns} turns  ·  L = ${eng(ind(), 'H', 2)}`, g.cx, SCENE.y + 32, 0.85, 'center', 14, ACC);

    // the current, on the wire, pointing where the electrons actually go
    const yBot = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 74;
    const moving = Math.abs(i) > 1e-6;
    const mx = (xLeft + g.x0) / 2 + 30;
    if (moving) {
      const dir = i > 0 ? -1 : 1; // electrons run against the conventional current
      ctx.strokeStyle = CUR;
      ctx.fillStyle = CUR;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      arrow(mx - dir * 36, yBot + 26, mx + dir * 36, yBot + 26, 8);
      label(`electrons: ${eng(Math.abs(i), 'A')}`, mx, yBot + 48, 0.8, 'center', 12, CUR);
    } else {
      label('nothing is moving yet', mx, yBot + 30, 0.5, 'center', 12);
    }

    const dIdt = vCoil() / ind();
    label(
      Math.abs(dIdt) < 1e-3
        ? 'steady current: the coil is just wire now'
        : `speeding up at ${eng(dIdt, 'A/s', 1)}`,
      SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 20,
      SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 18,
      0.55,
      'right',
      12,
      Math.abs(dIdt) < 1e-3 ? inkA(0.5) : WARM
    );
    if (isOpen() && !state.fly && Math.abs(i) > 1e-4)
      label('slow motion: this really takes microseconds', g.cx, SCENE.y + 54, 0.5, 'center', 11, WARM);
    drawLadder();
  }

  // --- scope -----------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScope() {
    panel(SCOPE, 'WHAT THE SOURCE DOES, AND WHAT THE CURRENT DOES');
    const px = SCOPE.x + 58, py = SCOPE.y + 22, pw = SCOPE.w - 78, ph = SCOPE.h - 58;
    const span = 10 * tauOn();
    const t1 = Math.max(span, histT), t0 = t1 - span;
    const X = (tt: number) => px + ((tt - t0) / span) * pw;
    let vmax = 0.5, imax = 1e-9;
    for (const h of hist) {
      vmax = Math.max(vmax, Math.abs(h.vs), Math.abs(h.vl));
      imax = Math.max(imax, Math.abs(h.i));
    }
    const Yv = (vv: number) => py + ph * 0.4 - (vv / vmax) * (ph * 0.34);
    const Yi = (ii: number) => py + ph * 0.85 - (ii / imax) * (ph * 0.13);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (const [y, txt] of [
      [Yv(0), '0 V'],
      [Yi(0), '0 A'],
    ] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.12);
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 3]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, y);
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(txt, px - 6, y + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
    label(`${vmax.toFixed(vmax > 100 ? 0 : 1)} V`, px - 6, Yv(vmax) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label(eng(imax, 'A', 1), px - 6, Yi(imax) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10, CUR);

    if (hist.length > 1) {
      const series: [string, (h: (typeof hist)[0]) => number, number][] = [
        [WARM, (h) => Yv(h.vs), 1.6],
        [ACC, (h) => Yv(h.vl), 2.2],
        [CUR, (h) => Yi(h.i), 1.8],
      ];
      for (const [col, fn, lw] of series) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = lw;
        ctx.beginPath();
        hist.forEach((h, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(h.t), fn(h)) : ctx.moveTo(X(h.t), fn(h))));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
    label('current', px + pw, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, CUR);
    label('coil', px + pw - 62, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, ACC);
    label('source', px + pw - 108, py + 12, 0.85, 'right', 11, WARM);
    label(`peak coil voltage ${eng(vPeak, 'V', 1)}`, px, py + ph + 18, 0.45, 'left', 10, WARM);
    label(`window = 10 τ = ${eng(10 * tauOn(), 's')}`, px + pw, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'right', 10);
  }

  // --- side panel ------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawSide() {
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      panel(SIDE, 'WHO LAGS WHOM');
      const cx = SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, cy = SIDE.y + 62, rad = 40;
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.14);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(cx, cy, rad, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
      const w = 2 * Math.PI * freqHz();
      const xl = w * ind();
      const theta = Math.atan2(xl, state.r); // how far the current lags
      const ang = -w * tAC;
      const arms: [number, number, string, string][] = [
        [ang, 1, WARM, 'source'],
        [ang - theta, 0.9, CUR, 'I'],
        [ang - theta + Math.PI / 2, Math.max(0.15, xl / Math.hypot(state.r, xl)), ACC, 'V_L'],
      ];
      for (const [a, len, col] of arms) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
        arrow(cx, cy, cx + Math.cos(a) * rad * len, cy + Math.sin(a) * rad * len, 7);
      }
      let lx = SIDE.x + 22;
      for (const [, , col, name] of arms) {
        ctx.fillStyle = col;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(lx, cy + rad + 16, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
        label(name, lx + 9, cy + rad + 20, 0.7, 'left', 10, col);
        lx += textWidth(name, 10) + 34;
      }
      label(
        `current lags by ${((theta * 180) / Math.PI).toFixed(0)}°`,
        SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2,
        SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 42,
        0.75,
        'center',
        12,
        CUR
      );
      label(`X_L = 2πfL = ${fmtR(xl)}`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 24, 0.55, 'center', 11);
      label(`at ${eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1)}`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, SIDE.y + SIDE.h - 8, 0.4, 'center', 10);
      return;
    }
    panel(SIDE, 'WHERE THE ENERGY WENT');
    const u = 0.5 * ind() * i * i;
    const top = SIDE.y + 30, x0 = SIDE.x + 100, bw = SIDE.w - 124;
    const scale = Math.max(1e-15, Math.abs(wSrc), u + wRes + wArc);
    const bars: [string, number, string][] = [
      ['source', wSrc, inkA(0.35)],
      ['in the field', u, FIELD],
      ['heat in R', wRes, WARM],
      [state.fly ? 'diode' : 'the spark', wArc, '#ef4444'],
    ];
    bars.forEach(([name, val, col], k) => {
      const y = top + k * 32;
      label(name, x0 - 10, y + 12, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
      rr(x0, y, bw, 15, 4);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      rr(x0, y, Math.max(1, (Math.abs(val) / scale) * bw), 15, 4);
      ctx.fill();
      label(eng(val, 'J', 2), x0 + bw - 8, y + 12, 0.75, 'right', 10);
    });
    label(`½LI² right now = ${eng(u, 'J', 2)}`, SIDE.x + SIDE.w / 2, top + 154, 0.6, 'center', 12, FIELD);
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    setRow(1, 'Current I', eng(i, 'A'));
    setRow(2, 'Across the coil V_L', eng(vCoil(), 'V'));
    setRow(3, 'Inductance L', eng(ind(), 'H'));
    if (state.src === 'ac') {
      setRow(4, 'Reactance X_L', fmtR(2 * Math.PI * freqHz() * ind()));
      setRow(5, 'Frequency', eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1));
    } else {
      setRow(4, 'Time constant τ = L/R', eng(tauOn(), 's'));
      setRow(5, 'Field inside B', eng(bField(), 'T', 3));
    }
    setRow(6, 'Flux linkage NΦ = LI', eng(ind() * i, 'Wb'));
    setRow(7, 'Energy ½LI²', eng(0.5 * ind() * i * i, 'J'));
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Inductor', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual'
        ? 'drive it yourself: the current will not jump, only ramp'
        : state.src === 'ac'
          ? 'the current is always a quarter cycle late'
          : 'a battery, a switch, and a coil that hates being cut off',
      20,
      52,
      0.5,
      'left',
      11,
      FIELD
    );
    const legend: [string, string][] = [
      [CUR, 'electron'],
      [FIELD, 'magnetic field'],
      [WARM, 'coil voltage'],
    ];
    let x = W - 20;
    for (let k = legend.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      const [c, tx] = legend[k];
      const tw = textWidth(tx, 11);
      label(tx, x, 30, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = c;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x - tw - 11, 26, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      x -= tw + 32;
    }
    drawScene();
    drawScope();
    drawSide();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dt = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dt));
    if (state.running) {
      clock += dt;
      physics(dt);
      // The queue moves at the current: speed is the whole meaning of I here.
      const vpx = Math.max(-900, Math.min(900, (i / Math.max(0.05, Math.abs(state.vs) / state.r)) * 190));
      train -= vpx * dt;
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', reset);

  let ready = false;
  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void, restart = false) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => {
      apply(+inp.value);
      if (restart && ready) reset();
    };
    inp.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('vs', (n) => {
    state.vs = n / 10;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(1)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('freq', (n) => {
    state.freq = n / 100;
    el('fval').textContent = eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1);
  });
  bindRange('r', (n) => {
    state.r = Math.round(10 * Math.pow(10, (n / 100) * 3)) / 10;
    el('rval').textContent = fmtR(state.r);
  }, true);
  bindRange('n', (n) => {
    state.turns = n;
    el('nval').textContent = String(n);
  }, true);
  bindRange('mu', (n) => {
    state.mur = Math.round(Math.pow(10, (n / 100) * 3.3));
    el('muval').textContent = String(state.mur);
  }, true);
  bindRange('a', (n) => {
    state.area = (n / 10) * 1e-4;
    el('aval').textContent = `${(n / 10).toFixed(1)} cm²`;
  }, true);
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });
  (el('fly') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.fly = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });
  (el('lines') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.lines = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });

  const show = (id: string, on: boolean) => {
    el(id).style.display = on ? '' : 'none';
  };
  function syncControls() {
    show('ctl-sw', state.src === 'dc');
    show('ctl-f', state.src === 'ac');
    el('vlab').textContent =
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'Drive it yourself' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'Amplitude' : 'Battery';
    el('vhint').textContent =
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'drag me up and down' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'peak volts' : 'battery volts';
    const inp = el('vs') as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.min = state.src === 'manual' ? '-120' : '0';
    if (state.src !== 'manual' && +inp.value <= 0) inp.value = '60';
    state.vs = +inp.value / 10;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(1)} V`;
    el('fval').textContent = eng(freqHz(), 'Hz', 1);
  }

  el('src').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#src button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.src = btn.dataset.s as 'manual' | 'dc' | 'ac';
    syncControls();
    reset();
  });
  el('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#mode button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.mode = btn.dataset.m as 'on' | 'off' | 'auto';
    if (state.mode !== 'auto') closed = state.mode === 'on';
    t = 0;
    if (!closed) vPeak = 0;
  });

  syncControls();
  reset();
  ready = true;
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .ind-canvas {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .check {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .check input {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
